# fixedbugs, defect 2036, 2026-10-13, a shape beside defect 2034's repair;
# pinned 2026-11-11 as a known cost by panel 245's R2 (provisional).
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own whose `printf(m)` takes its format
# from a variable holding `"hi\n"` is refused `ffi_header_refused` at exit
# 1, `format string is not a string literal (potentially insecure)
# [-Werror,-Wformat-security]`. Nothing in C makes the call undefined for the
# string `m` holds, which clang cannot see. Until panel 245 it built (it was
# `tests/golden/run/fixedbugs-2036-...-builds`), `-Wformat-security` passed
# over in the region.
#
# REASON: a door handing on the format it was given, `printf(f)`, is this
# same call to clang, and it read the stack's bytes for `n=%ld` at exit 0 and
# died of `%n` (defect 2465): no word tells the variable's string from the
# caller's, so the one form clang cannot judge is refused, and the census of
# 496 tracked programs binding a header met this case alone (panel 245's
# ffi-pragmatist).
#
# RULING: panel 245's R2, its S, provisional, author ratification pending:
# robustness first (design.md §1.12). The fix is a literal format,
# `printf("%s", m)` (`tests/golden/run/fixedbugs-2036-a-header-s-own-printf-of-a-variable-handed-as-a-string-builds`);
# this golden moves if the ruling does.

extern "fixedbugs-2036-a-header-s-own-printf-of-a-format-held-in-a-variable-is-a-known-cost.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function fmt_plain() -> i32

function main()
    print(fmt_plain())
